            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BARNKITTY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The name says it all! I did not have peanuts on hand, so substituted some peanut butter and used honey mustard (we like honey!). Chicken came out tender, juicy, and with a wonderful sweet/tangy flavor."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TMJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Husband loved it. actually went back for seconds. Used pecans instead of peanuts and crushed them until very small. Came out incredibly tender.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-28T18:20:30.803Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lricher"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy. Decreased the brown sugar to 1 1/2 tbsp. Added some salt to the sauce. Used thin sliced chicken breasts - 10 minutes, then flip and pour the rest of the sauce over it. 10 more minutes in the oven and it's done. Great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-18T15:28:14.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LIL_PYRO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So easy, and love that it uses readily available ingredients. Not too sweet.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-26T18:00:04.400Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Krazyquilts"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a couple tablespoons of minced garlic to the sauce and used cashews instead of peanuts because that's what I had. I also added onion chunks and about 2/3 of a bag of baby carrots around the chicken while it was cooking. The carrots and onions were *amazing*, some of the best I've ever had, but the chicken was just okay, very moist but rather bland. It might be better using boneless skinless chicken breasts instead of a whole chicken. I'd like to try this sauce with a whole chicken in the slow cooker, though. (Maybe it would absorb more of the flavor?) This sauce would also be great on pork. I will probably make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-13T18:49:21.123Z"
          },
